# Juggernaut - Next.js Dashboard Project Rules

## Documentation

📘 **[Design System](./docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md)** - Complete color palette, typography, spacing, and visual design standards
📘 **[Style Guide](./docs/STYLE_GUIDE.md)** - Component patterns, examples, and implementation details

## Project Context
- **Next.js Version**: 14.2.3 (App Router)
- **React Version**: 18.3.1
- **TypeScript**: Strict mode enabled
- **Primary Purpose**: Enterprise logistics dashboard with fleet management, trip tracking, and analytics

### Tech Stack
- **Framework**: Next.js 14 with App Router
- **UI Libraries**: Material-UI (MUI), Ant Design, Radix UI, shadcn/ui components
- **Styling**: CSS Modules + Tailwind utilities (hybrid approach)
- **State Management**: React Context (SnackbarProvider, custom hooks)
- **Data Fetching**: Axios with custom HTTP wrapper utilities
- **Date Handling**: Luxon, dayjs, date-fns (multiple libraries in use)
- **Maps**: Leaflet, React-Leaflet, Kepler.gl
- **Charts**: Recharts, Chart.js, ECharts, MUI Charts
- **Internationalization**: next-intl
- **Forms**: React Hook Form, react-datepicker
- **Icons**: Material-UI Icons, Lucide React, Ant Design Icons

---

## Directory Structure

```
src/
├── app/                    # Next.js App Router - all routes
│   ├── layout.tsx         # Root layout with providers
│   ├── page.tsx           # Home page
│   ├── globals.css        # Global CSS variables
│   ├── [feature]/         # Feature-based routing
│   │   ├── page.tsx       # Route page component
│   │   └── components/    # Feature-specific components (optional)
│   └── api/               # API routes
├── components/            # Reusable components organized by feature
│   ├── UI/               # Generic UI components (buttons, cards, etc.)
│   ├── [FeatureName]/    # Feature-specific components (PascalCase)
│   ├── Header/           # App header components
│   └── Drawer/           # Navigation drawer components
├── utils/                # Utility functions
│   ├── Communication.ts  # API client functions (httpsGet, httpsPost, httpsPut)
│   ├── dateUtils.ts      # Date manipulation utilities
│   ├── timeService.ts    # Time conversion utilities
│   ├── storageService.ts # Cookie/storage management
│   ├── helper.ts         # General helper functions
│   └── interface.ts      # Shared TypeScript interfaces
├── services/             # Service layer
│   └── Authenticator/    # Authentication service
├── hooks/                # Custom React hooks
│   └── snackBar.tsx      # Snackbar context and hook
├── lib/                  # Library utilities
│   └── utils.ts          # Utility helpers (cn function for classnames)
├── assets/               # Static assets (images, icons, SVGs)
├── environments/         # Environment configuration
└── MapsHelper/           # Map-related utilities
```

---

## Next.js Specific Rules

### App Router Conventions
- **ALL components are Client Components** - This project uses `"use client"` directive at the top of nearly every component
- No Server Components are currently used in this codebase
- Pages are located in `src/app/[feature]/page.tsx`
- No API routes are extensively used (uses external APIs via axios)

### File Naming
- **Pages**: `page.tsx` (lowercase)
- **Layouts**: `layout.tsx` (lowercase)
- **Components**: PascalCase (e.g., `MetricCard.tsx`, `VehicleTable.tsx`)
- **Utilities**: camelCase (e.g., `dateUtils.ts`, `helper.ts`)
- **CSS Modules**: `ComponentName.module.css`
- **Regular CSS**: `component.css` or `page.css`

### Client Components Pattern
```typescript
"use client"

import { useState, useEffect } from "react"
import { useRouter } from "next/navigation"

export default function FeaturePage() {
  // Component logic
}
```

### Routing
- Use Next.js App Router (`src/app/`)
- Navigation via `useRouter()` from `next/navigation`
- Route parameters via `useSearchParams()` for query strings
- Wrap components using `useSearchParams()` in `<Suspense>` boundary

### Image Optimization
- Use `next/image` with `Image` component
- Configure allowed domains in `next.config.mjs`
- Current allowed domains: `wagon-tally-sheet.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com`, `s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com`

### Environment Variables
- Environment-specific configurations in `src/environments/env.api.ts`
- Use `process.env.NODE_ENV` to differentiate environments (local, dev, production)
- No `.env` files pattern - configuration is in TypeScript files

---

## Component Patterns

### Standard Component Structure
```typescript
"use client"

import React from "react"
import styles from "./ComponentName.module.css"
import { SomeType } from "@/utils/interface"

interface ComponentNameProps {
  title: string
  value: string
  icon: React.ReactNode
  onAction?: () => void
}

const ComponentName: React.FC<ComponentNameProps> = ({
  title,
  value,
  icon,
  onAction
}) => {
  // Component logic

  return (
    <div className={styles.container}>
      {/* JSX */}
    </div>
  )
}

export default ComponentName
```

### Props Definition
- Define props interface immediately before component
- Use `React.FC<PropsType>` for functional components
- Props interfaces named `[ComponentName]Props`
- Use optional props with `?` for non-required props

### Component Export
- **Default exports** for components (not named exports)
- Exception: UI components may export both (e.g., `export { Button, buttonVariants }`)

### State Management
- Use `useState` for local component state
- Use `useEffect` for side effects and data fetching
- Use Context for global state (see `SnackbarProvider` example)
- Access context via custom hooks (e.g., `useSnackbar()`)

---

## Data Fetching Patterns

### API Communication
All API calls use custom HTTP utilities from `@/utils/Communication`:

```typescript
import { httpsGet, httpsPost, httpsPut } from "@/utils/Communication"
import { useRouter } from "next/navigation"

// GET request
const fetchData = async () => {
  const router = useRouter()
  const response = await httpsGet("endpoint/path", 0, router)
  return response?.data
}

// POST request
const createData = async (data: any) => {
  const router = useRouter()
  const response = await httpsPost("endpoint/path", data, router, 0)
  return response
}
```

### HTTP Utilities Parameters
- `httpsGet(path, type = 0, router)`
- `httpsPost(path, data, router = null, type = 0, isFile = false)`
- `httpsPut(path, data, router = null, type = 0, isFile = false)`
- `type` parameter selects API base URL (0-3 index)

### Authentication
- Auth token stored in cookies via `storageService`
- Authorization header: `bearer [token] shipper [shipper_id]`
- 401 responses redirect to login page
- Auth handled in `services/Authenticator/Auth.ts`

### Error Handling
- API errors caught in `.catch()` blocks
- 401 errors trigger automatic redirect to login
- Use `useSnackbar()` for user-facing error messages

---

## Styling Conventions

### Hybrid Approach
This project uses **CSS Modules + Tailwind utilities** (NOT pure Tailwind):

**CSS Modules (Primary)**:
```typescript
import styles from "./Component.module.css"

<div className={styles.container}>
  <h1 className={styles.title}>Title</h1>
</div>
```

**Tailwind Utilities (Secondary)**:
```typescript
// Used mainly in shadcn/ui components
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils"

<div className={cn("flex items-center gap-2", className)}>
```

**Material-UI Components**:
```typescript
import { Box, Grid, Container } from "@mui/material"

<Box sx={{ padding: 2, backgroundColor: 'primary.main' }}>
```

### CSS Module Patterns
- One `.module.css` file per component
- Class names in camelCase (e.g., `.metricCard`, `.cardHeader`)
- Import as `styles` object
- Use descriptive class names

### Global Styles
- Global CSS variables in `src/app/globals.css`:
  ```css
  :root {
    --primary-color: #2a9d8f;
    --secondary-color: #e76f51;
    --tertiary-color: #264653;
    --background-color: #f8f9fa;
    --card-background: #ffffff;
    --text-primary: #1a1a1a;
    --text-secondary: #6c757d;
    --border-color: #e9ecef;
  }
  ```

### Responsive Design
- Use MUI's `useMediaQuery` hook for responsive behavior
- Mobile-specific components in separate files (e.g., `MobileEWayBillDashboard`)
- Breakpoints via MUI theme: `theme.breakpoints.down("sm")`

---

## TypeScript Standards

### Strict Mode Enabled
```json
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "strict": true,
    "target": "es2020"
  }
}
```

### Type Organization
- Shared interfaces in `src/utils/interface.ts`
- Component-specific types defined inline with component
- Use `interface` for object shapes (preferred)
- Use `type` for unions, intersections, and utilities

### Common Patterns

**Props Interface**:
```typescript
interface MetricCardProps {
  title: string
  value: string
  trend?: "up" | "down" | "neutral"
  icon: React.ReactNode
}
```

**API Response Typing**:
```typescript
interface ShipmentData {
  _id: string
  status: {
    name: string
    code: string
  }
  // ... more fields
}
```

**Any Usage**:
- `any` is used extensively in existing code
- For new code, prefer specific types when possible
- Use `any` only when dealing with complex external library types

### Path Aliases
- Use `@/` alias for imports from `src/`
- Configured in `tsconfig.json`

**Example**:
```typescript
import { httpsGet } from "@/utils/Communication"
import Header from "@/components/Header/header"
import { useSnackbar } from "@/hooks/snackBar"
```

---

## Helper Functions Organization

### Utility Categories

**Communication** (`utils/Communication.ts`):
- `httpsGet(path, type, router)` - GET requests
- `httpsPost(path, data, router, type, isFile)` - POST requests
- `httpsPut(path, data, router, type, isFile)` - PUT requests
- `apiCall(config)` - Generic API call wrapper

**Date Utilities** (`utils/dateUtils.ts`):
- `toUTCString(date, startOfDay)` - Convert to UTC ISO string
- `formatDate(date, format)` - Format date string
- `getDayName(date, format)` - Get day name
- `generateDateRange(startDate, days, format)` - Generate date array
- `convertToUTC(date)` - Convert to UTC

**Time Service** (`utils/timeService.ts`):
- `utcToist(utc, format)` - UTC to IST conversion
- `utcToistTime(utc, format)` - UTC to IST time
- `getTimeWithAMPM(utc)` - Get time with AM/PM
- `convertMsToHM(milliseconds)` - Convert milliseconds to HH:MM
- Default export as service object

**Storage Service** (`utils/storageService.ts`):
- `setCookies(name, value, options)` - Set cookie
- `getCookie(name, path)` - Get cookie value
- `hasCookie(name, path)` - Check cookie exists
- `deleteCookie(name, options)` - Delete cookie
- `deleteAllCache(options)` - Clear all cookies

**CSV Export** (`utils/jsonToCsv.ts`):
- `jsontocsv(items, title, headers)` - Export JSON to CSV file

**Class Names** (`lib/utils.ts`):
- `cn(...inputs)` - Merge Tailwind classes using clsx + tailwind-merge

### Naming Conventions
- **Date/Time utilities**: `formatDate`, `convertToUTC`, `utcToist`
- **API utilities**: `httpsGet`, `httpsPost`, `httpsPut`
- **Storage utilities**: `setCookies`, `getCookie`, `deleteCookie`
- **Converters**: `convertToISO`, `convertMsToHM`, `jsontocsv`
- **Getters**: `getAuth`, `getCookie`, `getDayName`, `getToday`

### Documentation
- Use JSDoc comments for utility functions
- Include parameter descriptions and return types
- Example:
  ```typescript
  /**
   * Converts a date to UTC and returns it as an ISO string
   * @param date - Date string or dayjs object
   * @param startOfDay - If true, sets the time to start of day (00:00:00)
   * @returns UTC ISO string
   */
  export const toUTCString = (date: string | dayjs.Dayjs, startOfDay: boolean = true): string => {
    // Implementation
  }
  ```

